    },
    {
      "tool_id": "hirearchy::request",
      "description": "Ask a direct report for one of its services (see `services`): a task built from the contract.\n\n        inputs: {input name: value}; required ones must be present. note: free text for the owner. extra_acceptance:\n        criteria added after the contract's (the contract's always apply). budget: runs handed down (default: the\n        contract's; for a rework the user asked for, source=\"human\", what is left of the runs the user approved for the\n        case, at most the contract's, and 1 when nothing is left; the usual reserve rule applies). revises: id of an\n        earlier request of this service to send back for rework; the reply then states the case total (runs used by the\n        whole chain, the user's and your relayed reworks' apart, runs handed down, the contract's budget per request)\n        and tells you to inform the user when the user's requests cost more than they approved, and names the top-up to\n        ask for when a rework the user asked for gets less than a round of the team needs.\n        source (with revises): \"human\" when the user asked for this rework\n        (a rework after their own rejection, carrying their corrections, is one), \"relayed\" (the default) when it is your\n        own reading; the owner sees which.\n        base (with revises and source=\"human\"): \"delivered\" or \"latest\". When your own relayed rework changed a file after the\n        delivery the user judged, this is refused until you say which version the user's corrections apply to:\n        \"delivered\" (the lead restores the version they judged, then applies their corrections) or \"latest\" (your\n        relayed changes stay; tell the user).\n        Returns the task id; the result comes back like any result, then rate it with `feedback`.\n        ",
      "input_schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "service": {
            "title": "Service",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "inputs": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "additionalProperties": true,
                "type": "object"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Inputs"
          },
          "title": {
            "default": "",
            "title": "Title",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "note": {
            "default": "",
            "title": "Note",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "extra_acceptance": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "items": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "type": "array"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Extra Acceptance"
          },
